@startuml
title Bomberman - class diagram

' ==========================================
' Notation (UML)
'   - private   + public   # protected   ~ package (same Java package)
'   underlined = static, italic = abstract
'   A *-- B   composition: A owns B, B lives and dies with A
'   A --> B   association: A keeps a reference to B
'   A <|-- B  inheritance: B extends A (also interface extends interface)
'   A <|.. B  realization: B implements interface A
'   A ..> B   dependency: A uses or creates B
'   A -o Saveable   ball notation: A implements interface Saveable
'                   (used for Saveable only, which 7 classes implement,
'                   to avoid 7 long lines across the diagram)
' A field that refers to an object of another class is drawn as a line
' with the field name on it, not repeated in the box. Values (numbers,
' text, enums, Cell, Hitbox and collections of them) stay in the box.
' Lines marked [hidden] or [norank] only help the automatic layout.
' Colours match the MVC legend of the sequence diagrams.
' ==========================================
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor White
skinparam ClassBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ArrowColor SlateGray
skinparam PackageBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BorderColor Orange
}
hide empty members
set namespaceSeparator none

legend top right
  |<#E6E6E6> View (React / TypeScript) |
  |<#CFE3F7> Controller (Java) |
  |<#D8F0D8> Model (Java) |
  |<#FFFFFF> Class --o Saveable : the class implements Saveable (UML ball notation) |
endlegend

' ==========================================
' View (TypeScript, not Java): only shows where the controller is called from
' ==========================================
package "view (React / TypeScript)" #E6E6E6 {
    class GameLoop <<TypeScript>>
}
note right of GameLoop
  Not Java. Draws the canvas, plays sounds, turns
  keys into inputMask, shows the menus and the save
  list, keeps the saves and the top score in
  localStorage.
end note

' ==========================================
' Controller
' ==========================================
package "agh.po.bomberman.controller" #CFE3F7 {
    class GameBridge <<utility>> {
        {static} + loadStages(text : String) : boolean
        {static} + loadTopScore(bytes : byte[]) : void
        {static} + getTopScore() : int
        {static} + exportTopScore() : byte[]
        {static} + startNewGame() : void
        {static} + tick(inputMask : int) : void
        {static} + getState() : String
        {static} + pause() : void
        {static} + resume() : void
        {static} + quitToMenu() : void
        {static} + saveGame(name : String, existingNames : String[]) : SaveResult
        {static} + listSaves(names : String[], saves : byte[][]) : String
        {static} + loadGame(bytes : byte[]) : boolean
    }
    note left of GameBridge
      Only static members: TeaVM exports static
      methods (@JSExport) to JavaScript. Its four
      lines into the model are static fields.
      getState() and listSaves() return text (JSON),
      so no model class depends on TeaVM.
    end note

    class SaveResult <<value>> {
        - check : String
        - name : String
        - bytes : byte[]
        + SaveResult(check : String, name : String, bytes : byte[])
        + getCheck() : String
        + getName() : String
        + getBytes() : byte[]
    }
    note left of SaveResult
      Read by TypeScript, so it holds
      only text and bytes. check: "OK",
      "EMPTY", "TOO_LONG" or "TAKEN";
      name: the trimmed name to store
      the save under; bytes: only when
      check is "OK".
    end note
}

' ==========================================
' Model
' ==========================================
package "agh.po.bomberman.model" #D8F0D8 {

    class Game {
        - random : Random
        - state : GameState
        - stageNumber : int
        - lives : int
        - score : int
        - introTimer : int
        - deathTimer : int
        - stageCleared : boolean
        {static} + START_LIVES : int = 2
        {static} + LAST_STAGE : int = 50
        {static} + INTRO_TICKS : int = 180
        {static} + DEATH_TICKS : int = 180
        --
        + Game(stageTable : StageTable, highScore : HighScore)
        {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream, stageTable : StageTable,\n      highScore : HighScore) : Game
        + update(input : Input) : void
        + pause() : void
        + resume() : void
        + quit() : void
        + save(out : DataOutputStream, name : String, savedAt : long) : void
        + onEnemyKilled(points : int) : void
        + onPlayerHit() : void
        + onStageCleared() : void
        + getState() : GameState
        + getStageNumber() : int
        + getLives() : int
        + getScore() : int
        + getPlayer() : Player
        + getStage() : Stage
        - setUpStage() : void
        - nextStage() : void
        - finishDeath() : void
    }

    enum GameState {
        STAGE_INTRO
        PLAYING
        PAUSED
        DYING
        GAME_OVER
        WON
    }

    interface StageListener {
        + onEnemyKilled(points : int) : void
        + onPlayerHit() : void
        + onStageCleared() : void
    }

    interface Arena {
        + isPassable(cell : Cell, mover : Creature) : boolean
        + lookForPlayer(enemy : Enemy) : Direction
        + playerCell() : Cell
        + random() : Random
    }

    class Stage {
        - random : Random
        - timeLeft : int
        - cleared : boolean
        - pendingWaves : Set<Cell>
        - events : List<GameEvent>
        {static} + TIME_LIMIT : int = 18600
        {static} + MAX_ENEMIES : int = 10
        --
        + Stage(stageData : StageData, board : Board, enemies : List<Enemy>,\n      player : Player, listener : StageListener, random : Random)
        {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream, stageData : StageData,\n      player : Player, listener : StageListener, random : Random) : Stage
        + update(input : Input) : void
        + isPassable(cell : Cell, mover : Creature) : boolean
        + lookForPlayer(enemy : Enemy) : Direction
        + playerCell() : Cell
        + random() : Random
        + noEnemiesLeft() : boolean
        + livingEnemyCount() : int
        + getTimeLeft() : int
        + getBoard() : Board
        + getEnemies() : List<Enemy>
        + getBombs() : List<Bomb>
        + getExplosions() : List<Explosion>
        + drainEvents() : List<GameEvent>
        + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        - updatePlayer(input : Input) : void
        - placeBomb() : void
        - detonate() : void
        - updateBombs() : void
        - explode(bomb : Bomb) : void
        - spawnPendingWaves() : void
        - updateTimer() : void
        - updateEnemies() : void
        - isBurning(cell : Cell) : boolean
    }
    Stage -() Saveable

    class Input {
        - mask : int
        - previousMask : int
        - direction : Direction
        {static} + UP : int = 1
        {static} + DOWN : int = 2
        {static} + LEFT : int = 4
        {static} + RIGHT : int = 8
        {static} + BOMB : int = 16
        {static} + DETONATE : int = 32
        --
        + update(mask : int) : void
        + getDirection() : Direction
        + bombPressed() : boolean
        + detonatePressed() : boolean
    }

    enum GameEvent {
        BOMB_PLACED
        BOMB_EXPLODED
        ENEMY_KILLED
        POWER_UP_TAKEN
        PLAYER_DIED
        WAVE_SPAWNED
        TIME_UP
        STAGE_CLEARED
    }

    class HighScore {
        - topScore : int
        + HighScore()
        {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : HighScore
        + submit(score : int) : void
        + getTopScore() : int
        + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
    }
    HighScore -() Saveable

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.board" {
        class Board {
            - tiles : Tile[][]
            - crumbleTicks : Map<Cell, Integer>
            - doorCell : Cell
            - powerUpCell : Cell
            {static} + WIDTH : int = 31
            {static} + HEIGHT : int = 13
            {static} + START : Cell = new Cell(1, 1)
            {static} + CRUMBLE_TICKS : int = 30
            --
            + Board(width : int, height : int)
            {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : Board
            + tileAt(cell : Cell) : Tile
            + placeSoftBlock(cell : Cell) : void
            + hideDoor(cell : Cell) : void
            + hidePowerUp(cell : Cell, powerUp : PowerUp) : void
            + crumble(cell : Cell) : void
            + tick() : void
            + exposedItemAt(cell : Cell) : Item
            + takeItem(cell : Cell) : PowerUp
            + removeItem(cell : Cell) : void
            + getPowerUp() : PowerUp
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }
        Board -() Saveable

        enum Tile {
            FREE
            HARD
            SOFT
            CRUMBLING
        }

        enum Item {
            NONE
            DOOR
            POWER_UP
        }

        class Cell <<value>> {
            - col : int
            - row : int
            + Cell(col : int, row : int)
            + col() : int
            + row() : int
            + next(direction : Direction) : Cell
            + equals(other : Object) : boolean
            + hashCode() : int
        }

        enum Direction {
            UP
            DOWN
            LEFT
            RIGHT
            NONE
            --
            - dx : int
            - dy : int
            + dx() : int
            + dy() : int
            + opposite() : Direction
        }
    }

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.creature" {
        abstract class Creature {
            - x : int
            - y : int
            - subPixel : double
            - alive : boolean
            + getX() : int
            + getY() : int
            + centerCell() : Cell
            + isAtCellCenter() : boolean
            + isFullyInside(cell : Cell) : boolean
            + overlaps(cell : Cell) : boolean
            + hitbox() : Hitbox
            + isAlive() : boolean
            + die() : void
            + {abstract} passesSoftBlocks() : boolean
            + {abstract} passesBombs() : boolean
            # {abstract} speed() : double
            # stepThisTick() : int
            # moveBy(dx : int, dy : int) : void
            # placeAt(cell : Cell) : void
            # revive() : void
            # writeBaseState(out : DataOutputStream) : void
            # readBaseState(in : DataInputStream) : void
        }
        Creature -() Saveable

        class Player {
            - bombCapacity : int
            - fireRange : int
            - speedUp : boolean
            - wallPass : boolean
            - bombPass : boolean
            - flamePass : boolean
            - detonator : boolean
            - invincibleTicks : int
            {static} + MAX_BOMBS : int = 10
            {static} + MAX_FIRE_RANGE : int = 5
            {static} + INVINCIBLE_TICKS : int = 2040
            --
            + Player()
            {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : Player
            + move(direction : Direction, arena : Arena) : void
            + tick() : void
            + respawnAt(cell : Cell) : void
            + getBombCapacity() : int
            + getFireRange() : int
            + hasDetonator() : boolean
            + isInvincible() : boolean
            + isFireProof() : boolean
            + passesSoftBlocks() : boolean
            + passesBombs() : boolean
            + increaseBombCapacity() : void
            + increaseFireRange() : void
            + grantSpeed() : void
            + grantWallPass() : void
            + grantBombPass() : void
            + grantFlamePass() : void
            + grantDetonator() : void
            + startInvincibility() : void
            + loseTemporaryPowerUps() : void
            # speed() : double
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }

        class Enemy {
            - type : EnemyType
            - direction : Direction
            - directionTimer : int
            - deathTicks : int
            --
            ~ Enemy(type : EnemyType, strategy : MovementStrategy)
            ~ Enemy(type : EnemyType, strategy : MovementStrategy, cell : Cell)
            ~ readState(in : DataInputStream) : void
            + move(arena : Arena) : void
            + die() : void
            + tickDeath() : boolean
            + getPoints() : int
            + getType() : EnemyType
            + getDirection() : Direction
            + timerRanOut() : boolean
            + resetTimer(random : Random) : void
            + passesSoftBlocks() : boolean
            + passesBombs() : boolean
            # speed() : double
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }

        enum EnemyType {
            BALLOM
            ONIL
            DALL
            MINVO
            OVAPI
            KONDORIA
            PARSE
            PONTAN
            --
            - speed : double
            - minTimer : int
            - maxTimer : int
            - points : int
            - wallPass : boolean
            + speed() : double
            + hasTimer() : boolean
            + randomTimer(random : Random) : int
            + points() : int
            + wallPass() : boolean
        }

        class EnemyFactory <<utility>> {
            {static} + create(type : EnemyType, cell : Cell) : Enemy
            {static} + createWave(type : EnemyType, cell : Cell, count : int) : List<Enemy>
            {static} + readEnemy(in : DataInputStream) : Enemy
            {static} - strategyFor(type : EnemyType) : MovementStrategy
        }

        class Hitbox <<value>> {
            - x : int
            - y : int
            - size : int
            + Hitbox(x : int, y : int, size : int)
            + overlaps(other : Hitbox) : boolean
        }
    }

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.ai" {
        interface MovementStrategy {
            + chooseDirection(enemy : Enemy, arena : Arena) : Direction
            + onBlocked(enemy : Enemy, arena : Arena) : Direction
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
            + readState(in : DataInputStream) : void
        }
        class RandomWalk
        class AxisChaser {
            - watchesRow : boolean
            - watchesColumn : boolean
            + AxisChaser(watchesRow : boolean, watchesColumn : boolean)
        }
        class Alternating {
            - towardPlayer : boolean
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
            + readState(in : DataInputStream) : void
        }
        class JunctionWalker
        class Pursuer
    }
    note bottom of MovementStrategy
      Strategy pattern. Every class below implements
      chooseDirection() and onBlocked() ("Move Enemies").
      writeTo() and readState() are default methods that
      do nothing; only Alternating has state to save.
    end note

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.bomb" {
        class Bomb {
            - cell : Cell
            - fireRange : int
            - fuseTicks : int
            {static} + FUSE_TICKS : int = 160
            {static} + NO_FUSE : int = -1
            --
            + Bomb(cell : Cell, fireRange : int, fuseTicks : int)
            {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : Bomb
            + tick() : boolean
            + getCell() : Cell
            + getFireRange() : int
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }
        Bomb -() Saveable

        class Explosion {
            - center : Cell
            - fireRange : int
            - flameCells : Set<Cell>
            - brokenBlocks : Set<Cell>
            - ticksLeft : int
            - killCount : int
            {static} + DURATION : int = 30
            --
            + Explosion(center : Cell, fireRange : int)
            {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : Explosion
            + spread(board : Board, bombs : List<Bomb>) : void
            + getFlameCells() : Set<Cell>
            + getHitCells() : Set<Cell>
            + getHitBombs() : List<Bomb>
            + burns(cell : Cell) : boolean
            + scoreKill(basePoints : int) : int
            + tick() : boolean
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }
        Explosion -() Saveable
    }

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.powerup" {
        interface PowerUp {
            + applyTo(player : Player) : void
            + getType() : PowerUpType
            {static} + of(type : PowerUpType) : PowerUp
        }
        enum PowerUpType {
            BOMB
            FIRE
            SPEED
            WALL_PASS
            BOMB_PASS
            FLAME_PASS
            DETONATOR
            MYSTERY
        }
        class BombUp
        class FireUp
        class SpeedUp
        class WallPass
        class BombPass
        class FlamePass
        class Detonator
        class Mystery
    }
    note bottom of PowerUp
      Every class below implements applyTo() and
      getType(). They are package-private, so the
      static factory method PowerUp.of(type) is the
      only way to create one.
    end note

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.setup" {
        class StageTable {
            {static} + parse(text : String) : StageTable
            + get(stageNumber : int) : StageData
        }
        class StageData <<value>> {
            - stageNumber : int
            - enemies : Map<EnemyType, Integer>
            - powerUpType : PowerUpType
            - waveType : EnemyType
            + StageData(stageNumber : int, enemies : Map<EnemyType, Integer>,\n      powerUpType : PowerUpType, waveType : EnemyType)
            + stageNumber() : int
            + enemies() : Map<EnemyType, Integer>
            + powerUpType() : PowerUpType
            + waveType() : EnemyType
            + softBlockCount() : int
        }
        class StageFactory <<utility>> {
            {static} + create(stageData : StageData, player : Player,\n      listener : StageListener, random : Random) : Stage
            {static} - startArea() : Set<Cell>
        }
    }

    ' ------------------------------------------
    package "model.save" {
        interface Saveable {
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }
        class SaveHeader {
            - name : String
            - savedAt : long
            - stageNumber : int
            - lives : int
            - score : int
            - damaged : boolean
            {static} + SAVE_VERSION : int = 1
            {static} + NEWEST_FIRST : Comparator<SaveHeader>
            --
            + SaveHeader(name : String, savedAt : long, stageNumber : int,\n      lives : int, score : int)
            {static} + readFrom(in : DataInputStream) : SaveHeader
            {static} + damaged(name : String) : SaveHeader
            + getName() : String
            + getSavedAt() : long
            + getStageNumber() : int
            + getLives() : int
            + getScore() : int
            + isDamaged() : boolean
            + writeTo(out : DataOutputStream) : void
        }
        SaveHeader -() Saveable
        class SaveName <<utility>> {
            {static} + MAX_LENGTH : int = 20
            {static} + check(name : String, existingNames : String[]) : NameCheck
        }
        enum NameCheck {
            OK
            EMPTY
            TOO_LONG
            TAKEN
        }
    }
}

' ==========================================
' Relationships
' ==========================================
' MVC: the view calls only the controller, the controller calls the
' model, and the model knows neither of them.
GameLoop ..> GameBridge : calls
GameBridge .left.> SaveResult : returns
GameBridge --> "0..1" Game : game
GameBridge --> "1" StageTable : stageTable
GameBridge --> "1" HighScore : highScore
GameBridge --> "1" Input : input
GameBridge ..> SaveName : checks names
GameBridge ..> SaveHeader : lists saves

' Game and its stage (Observer: the stage reports to a StageListener)
Game .right.|> StageListener
Game *-- "1" Stage : stage
Game *-- "1" Player : player
Game --> "1" StageTable : stageTable
Game --> "1" HighScore : highScore
Game ..> StageFactory : sets up stages
Game ..> SaveHeader : writes / reads

Stage .right.|> Arena
Stage --> "1" StageListener : listener
Stage --> "1" StageData : stageData
Stage --> "1" Player : player
Stage *-- "1" Board : board
Stage *-- "0..*\n{ordered}" Bomb : bombs
Stage --> "0..*\n{ordered}" Bomb : explosionQueue
Stage *-- "0..*" Explosion : explosions
Stage *-- "0..*" Enemy : enemies
Stage ..> EnemyFactory : waves, Pontans

Board *-- "0..1" PowerUp : powerUp

' Creatures
Creature <|-- Player
Creature <|-- Enemy
Enemy *-- "1" MovementStrategy : strategy
Arena <.. Player : asks where to walk
Arena <.. Enemy : asks where to walk
Arena <.. MovementStrategy : looks around
EnemyFactory ..> Enemy : creates
EnemyFactory ..> MovementStrategy : creates

' Strategy pattern
MovementStrategy <|.. RandomWalk
MovementStrategy <|.. AxisChaser
MovementStrategy <|.. Alternating
MovementStrategy <|.. JunctionWalker
MovementStrategy <|.. Pursuer

' Power-ups
PowerUp <|.. BombUp
PowerUp <|.. FireUp
PowerUp <|.. SpeedUp
PowerUp <|.. WallPass
PowerUp <|.. BombPass
PowerUp <|.. FlamePass
PowerUp <|.. Detonator
PowerUp <|.. Mystery
PowerUp ..> Player : upgrades

' Bombs
Explosion ..> Board : spreads over
Explosion --> "0..*" Bomb : hitBombs

' Stage setup (Factory)
StageTable *-- "50" StageData : stages
StageFactory ..> Stage : creates
StageFactory ..> Board : creates
StageFactory ..> PowerUp : PowerUp.of
StageFactory ..> EnemyFactory : uses

' Saving: the classes that implement Saveable carry a ball (see the
' packages); interface MovementStrategy extends it.
Saveable <|-[norank]- MovementStrategy

' Layout only (no meaning): power-ups in two rows
BombUp -[hidden]down- WallPass
FireUp -[hidden]down- BombPass
SpeedUp -[hidden]down- FlamePass
Detonator -[hidden]down- Mystery

@enduml
